CORRECTIONS
1. §1 intro "every dynamic and static vertex carries both prevPos and pos" -> only DynamicVertex has prevPos; StaticVertex has pos only (StaticVertex.cs:7-26). Moving geometry is removed from the static set and drawn dynamically.
2. §3.6 "Requires SwitchCount (3) consecutive samples on one side before switching" -> SwitchCount is read but has no effect as coded: both override branches at BspHeuristics.cs:62-65 are unreachable, because below/above counters reset each other and shouldUseBsp already matches the side. Switching happens on the first median sample that crosses the threshold outside the hysteresis band. Settings table row updated to match.
3. §3.2 inference "~90°-wide wedges at each side of the true FOV (at 90° FOV)" -> about 45° per side (90° in total). The near-plane half-space is about 180°, and (180-90)/2 = 45.
4. §1 item 1 "view is inside or above a Boom transfer-heights sector" -> above or below the fake planes (TransferHeightView Top/Bottom). Added that for Middle view the result comes from UseBspBasedOnHeuristic (Bsp->true, Static->false), BspHeuristics.cs:19-34.
5. GeometryTextureLookup.cs:33-55 (file is 29 lines) -> GeometryTextureLookup.cs:18-28; TextureGeometryLookup.cs:6-27 -> 6-26.
6. Sky/Sphere/SkySphereComponent.cs:182-201 (file is 86 lines) -> 50-69.
7. UZDoom CheckUpdate(screen->mVertexData, sector) cited hw_bsp.cpp:820-823 -> 794-797 (820-823 is the sector validcount block for things).
8. GeometryRenderer.cs:432-433 (seg-vs-clipper comment) -> 433-434.
9. WorldBase.cs:1041-1101 -> 1042-1102; added that GameTicker also increments while paused (1047).
10. IterateBlockmap excerpt was condensed and non-verbatim ("if (m_renderStatic) RenderSides(...)" on one line, "...RenderEntity") -> replaced with verbatim LegacyWorldRenderer.cs:155-175.
11. §2.3 cell count "up to about 24x24 = 576 cells" -> 24-25 cells per axis (~576-625), since 12000/512 = 23.4 and the box is not cell-aligned.
12. §3.6 "A position is queued every world tick [SinglePlayerWorld.cs:231-236]" -> offered every tick (230-236); in Adaptive mode it is enqueued only if the queue is empty (AutomapMarker.cs:108-112). Added that the stopwatch covers a dequeue batch (AutomapMarker.cs:124,178).
13. §5 "static VBO per sky component [SkyGeometryManager.cs; StaticCache...cs:565-636]" -> persistent per-component VBO (a StreamVertexBuffer, not GL static) patched with UploadSubData; cites SkyGeometryManager.cs:39-72,127-157 and StaticCacheGeometryRenderer.cs:565-611.
